00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.260
Walc François

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:20.300
belongs to this repertoire of

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.300
street musicians, singers

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.559
who wanted to survive

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.749
during German occupation

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.260
in Warsaw.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:31.730
Using

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.600
hits from pre-war

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:35.650
time

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:37.779
to make a living

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:39.500
to survive.

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:41.670
And in many cases, these

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.079
hits came

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.080
from abroad to Poland.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.140
That was the case of

00:07:47.872 --> 00:07:48.872
"Cielito Lindo."

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:51.520
But this is not the case of Walc

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:52.880
François. It

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:55.809
originated from this very

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:56.810
unique milieu

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:59.379
of pre-war

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.109
Polish Jewish artistic

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.110
circles

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:05.240
on the turn of 19,

00:08:06.119 --> 00:08:07.119
20 centuries.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:09.850
And there are some

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.789
special characters

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.479
of this story which I

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:16.450
would like to

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.969
say a few words about.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:20.559
The first is

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.520
Adam Karasiński, a

00:08:24.347 --> 00:08:25.510
Polish musician and composer

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:28.980
who is the author of Walc

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:30.800
François.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:32.040
It was

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:34.310
the year of 1905.

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:37.649
A reception

00:08:38.529 --> 00:08:40.349
devoted to his

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.159
mus-- colleague, the

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:43.619
composer and friend.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.640
And on that

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.900
very party, he,

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:49.660
for the first time performs this

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:51.250
melody of Walc François,

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.640
which quickly gain

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:57.260
in popularity and

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.148
became one of the main

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:02.510
Polish waltz melodies.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.610
And the Karasiński

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.289
was called the King of

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:07.319
Polish waltz, at that

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.360
time.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:12.010
He died in 1920.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.480
And he,

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:17.192
so there is, we have a family,

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:18.710
Polish Jewish family.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.869
His wife was Jewish and

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.420
the son, Zbigniew Karasiński,

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.980
became a new editor,

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:29.140
now author of new version of

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.740
this song in 1920.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.100
Zbigniew Karasiński is

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:37.100
a very, very interesting

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:38.959
personality.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:40.730
He became one of the

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:43.280
pioneers of

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:44.370
Polish jazz.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:48.079
And before the war,

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.239
during the war and after the war

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.879
time, he was very engaged in

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:53.880
developing

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.650
the orchestra's compositions.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.569
Concerts devoted to

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.079
mostly jazz music.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.479
Also popular music.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:04.219
But when

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:05.640
the year 1968 came,

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:09.200
this anti-Semitic

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.060
action by the

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:13.699
communist regime in Poland, he

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:14.700
emigrated

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:16.759
abroad. So

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.420
this is one,

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.759
one part of that story from

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:23.760
the Karasiński's

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:27.239
family and

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:29.640
another character very important,

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:30.915
it may be the crucial one

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:34.259
for the popularity of our song.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.358
It's Andrzej Włast,

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:39.850
a

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.529
Polish Jew coming

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:44.530
from Łódź who

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:46.709
came to Warsaw

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:50.310
at that time, and

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:52.259
it became one

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:53.926
of the major figures of developing

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.520
so-called Polish mass culture

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.274
with radios, cover ads and

00:10:58.890 --> 00:10:59.890
so on.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.342
Many people consider him the

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:02.920
first

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.999
person who who

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:08.030
was confident about

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.189
the need of mass

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:12.450
culture in a

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:14.949
new postwar post

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:16.570
First World War, Poland

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:19.090
at that time.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.689
So firstly, he started to cooperate

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:23.386
with the most famous and I think

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:25.379
the best cover we had

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:27.043
in pre-war time in Poland quid pro

00:11:27.044 --> 00:11:28.979
quo  was such

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:29.980
names

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:32.140
as Julian Tuwim

00:11:32.961 --> 00:11:33.961
and Hemar.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:35.877
Comparing to Andrzej Włast

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.599
as they were more ambitious,

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:40.530
the poetry, the lyrics

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:43.940
was on that higher level.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:44.980
But Andrzej Włas

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:50.280
like to compose

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:52.920
and to produce

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.010
more, popular

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:57.420
repertoire, less ambitious.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.879
That's why he was called

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.770
"Król Szmiry" in

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:05.009
pre war Warsaw, the king

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:06.419
of Szmira, which is a

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:09.150
less than ambitious repertoire

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:10.555
softly saying.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:12.820
But

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.340
there were, of course, the purest of

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.860
poetry in his lyrics

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:17.900
as well.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.409
He was an author of such songs

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:21.420
as "Rebeka",

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.050
very popular.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:26.019
Also after the war, especially when

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:28.210
Ewa Demarczyk started to perform it,

00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:30.400
and he he was the author

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:32.675
of the,

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:34.619
the lyrics to

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:36.090
Walc François.

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:40.020
And it became a hit

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:42.460
of a new cover that he established

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:44.819
in 1927 in Warsaw,

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:45.820
which was called

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:50.670
"Morskie Oko", "Sea eye".

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.020
Which was called

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:56.620
Warsaw's,

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.100
Casino de Paris,

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:02.380
because it was

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.340
influenced very heavily

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.090
by the French

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.309
tradition of

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:09.730
rewja and cabaret,

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.113
especially Casino de Paris also

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:14.670
Moulin Rouge and others.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.009
He was traveling very often to Paris

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.210
at that time and

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.939
taking the models and the

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:24.030
the inspiration from that tradition.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.380
And it was very much about

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.380
these culture in Warsaw,

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:30.650
it was a very much French oriented.

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:31.710
And

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.669
that was also the reason that Warsaw

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.950
was called at that time, the Paris

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:37.980
of the North.

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:40.579
And Andrzej Włast was

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:42.200
very responsible for

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.909
for that title.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:46.339
And we, we may understand why

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:48.167
it was called Walc François,

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.869
the French culture was very

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:52.980
attractive and

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.940
at the background of

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:57.180
this

00:13:58.340 --> 00:13:59.340
music.

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:02.300
Andrzej Włast

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.105
also composed,

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:12.119
he was the author of such

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.120
hits

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.575
as a lyrics

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:19.251
writer as "Tango Milonka,"

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:21.690
is the

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.040
most popular composition

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.836
at that time coming from Poland,

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.010
composed by Jerzy Petersburski.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:33.468
And with international

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.659
fame among

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:37.768
the singers performing

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.190
this composition was Édith

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:41.500
Piaf.

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:42.910
And

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:46.380
it was also performed on Broadway

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:47.470
in

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:51.340
Al Jolson Music halls.

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:56.560
So very successful hit

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:58.340
coming also from that

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:01.380
milieu in Warsaw.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.940
The, this,

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:09.220
worthwhile to mention also

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:11.540
very tragic fate of

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.419
Andrzej Włast during the

00:15:14.949 --> 00:15:16.799
Holocaust. He, he was

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.959
closed in Warsaw Ghetto.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:23.009
And there are different variants

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.800
of his death, one

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:26.820
of them is saying that

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:29.450
his friends make

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.589
the whole action to

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:33.442
take him out from the Warsaw

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:36.149
ghetto. But when

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:38.490
he saw German soldiers,

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:39.696
he went to panic and was

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:41.470
shot down at

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:43.500
the spot.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.150
We don't know exactly how

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:49.117
how it was, but he

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.059
perished in that

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:54.060
time in Warsaw.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.650
What about

00:15:58.210 --> 00:15:59.210
the

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:02.920
later

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.840
history of our

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:06.960
song, it

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.459
is still popular

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:11.809
in Poland.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.639
You may find it

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.220
in such productions

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:18.259
as the

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.260
TV series, "God

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:22.730
lining" "Boża Podszewka",

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:26.539
very popular in Poland in the 90s

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:29.969
of recent of last century.

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:32.260
But mainly the

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:36.060
living off of this

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:38.919
song and composition

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:41.910
is

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:44.365
because it's

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:47.689
popularity is because

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:50.013
the performance, by Tadeusz Kantor

00:16:50.014 --> 00:16:51.616
of that

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:53.679
class, from

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.160
1975.

00:16:57.770 --> 00:16:59.629
And there is an anecdote

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:01.489
behind it, why Kantor

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:03.541
used this melody

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:05.359
in his performance

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:08.059
was it his wife, Maria

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:09.090
Stangret,

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.469
who was humming

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:13.999
during the

00:17:17.449 --> 00:17:18.779
presence in one of the Kraków

00:17:20.239 --> 00:17:22.519
café, humming this melody

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.290
and kind of immediately said,

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.171
"Oh this is the melody for

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:28.450
our performance." Why

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:30.800
I think that it was

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:33.260
the whole performance,

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:35.209
which is one of the most

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:36.990
important performance of 20th

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:39.350
century, not only Polish theater.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.290
The reason for that,

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.410
I think, is that the

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:46.519
whole performance is about coming

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:48.350
back to our childhood time,

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:49.969
to our school time,

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:52.420
to revolve the memories,

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:54.290
of some traumatic memories from

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:56.929
the very time.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:59.030
And this melody serves

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:01.499
on that there in

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.370
that, in

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:04.980
this case, very

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:07.970
strongly.

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:10.329
So when we think today

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:12.210
about the Walc François,

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:15.249
it's very much about coming

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.469
back to our childhood,

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.479
to our past

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:21.969
with nostalgia, with kind

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:23.629
of feeling that

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:25.929
we we still

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:26.930
have of

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:28.800
returning to better

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:31.010
times, to the

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:34.210
golden age, something

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:37.030
like that. And precisely

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.180
that was

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.056
the reason Kantor used

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:44.079
forces, very dramatic performers.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:46.150
And, and that is, there is no

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:48.099
other music in that performance,

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:49.940
only it's like like light motif,

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.730
from the beginning to the end.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:53.560
Repeated and repeated in that

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:55.419
performance and

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.869
almost conducted by

00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:58.880
Kantor who was

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:01.930
present on the stage

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:03.060
and,

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.450
and conducting

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:08.049
this music.

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:11.650
So we still keep it

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:14.590
in our minds, in our hearts,

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.419
in our culture.

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:18.117
And we should remember,

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:21.310
mostly, I sing the last

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.439
verses of the song, which

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:25.180
goes "Gdyby zbudził w sercach złych

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:27.390
ludzi, Czar modnego

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:28.400
Walca François",

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:31.051
"If only it would evoke in these

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:32.440
hearts of evil, the

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:34.840
magic of that

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:36.260
French waltz".

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:38.920
I think we should still

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.170
do our best

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:43.659
to keep it, to keep this magic,

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:46.980
to counter the evil in our hearts.

